{"assets":["/statement-assets/f4d9ac4f3a6e79a6848cdc294b1b95ec6b907414a9b5e39e0c05f0aad9d3f20d.png","/statement-assets/f77e4e33aef4fc1b601680dde2f66e31c03e6d290446e04560d999bb22a39e1f.png","/statement-assets/8646386467390facc9d56da8df19e2498c713422f67c2e7310d0c69f31040b7c.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"457","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Golden System"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Piegirl got bored with binary, decimal and other integer based counting systems. Recently she discovered some interesting properties about number "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/f4d9ac4f3a6e79a6848cdc294b1b95ec6b907414a9b5e39e0c05f0aad9d3f20d.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", in particular that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q2 = q + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", and she thinks it would make a good base for her new unique system. She called it \"golden system\". In golden system the number is a non-empty string containing 0's and 1's as digits. The decimal value of expression "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a0a1...an"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals to "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/f77e4e33aef4fc1b601680dde2f66e31c03e6d290446e04560d999bb22a39e1f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Soon Piegirl found out that this system doesn't have same properties that integer base systems do and some operations can not be performed on it. She wasn't able to come up with a fast way of comparing two numbers. She is asking for your help."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given two numbers written in golden system notation, determine which of them has larger decimal value."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input consists of two lines — one for each number. Each line contains non-empty string consisting of '0' and '1' characters. The length of each string does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"100000"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if the first number is larger, \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"<"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if it is smaller and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"="}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if they are equal."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1000\n111\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"<\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"00100\n11\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"=\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"110\n101\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":">\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example first number equals to "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/8646386467390facc9d56da8df19e2498c713422f67c2e7310d0c69f31040b7c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", while second number is approximately "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1.6180339882 + 1.618033988 + 1 ≈ 5.236"},{"kind":"text","text":", which is clearly a bigger number."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example numbers are equal. Each of them is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" ≈ 2.618"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"457A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/457/problem/A"}